# desc: DFlash2 draft instead of the MTP head - MEASURED on the GB10 2026-10-28: 56.7 tok/s decode vs 41.2 for MTP=3 (K=4, mean acceptance ~2.4); needs docker build for patch 23
#
# History: the 2026-10-27 GB10 boot showed method=dflash resolving DFlash2DraftModel and the
# YaRN/max_model_len plumbing working, then dying at "Qwen4Exp speculative decoding supports
# only its native MTP checkpoint and linear n-gram proposers" (config.py allowlist = blocker 4 of
# https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/56088). Patch 23 (src/patch_dflash_qwen4exp.py)
# opened the allowlist, mounted the EAGLE-3-style target aux-hidden-state capture (incoai's
# completed-layer HC-mean recipe from the draft repo's qwen38-dflash2-capture.patch) and ported
# the QSA ring widening (vllm#54912). Rebuild the image after pulling:
#   docker build -t qwen38-flash-dgx:v0.32 .
# Measured result (GB10 TP1, hybrid, YaRN 500k, this profile, 2026-10-28): bench/perf.py
# decode 56.7 tok/s median (54.5-56.9), TTFT 197 ms, deterministic, prefix caching healthy;
# SpecDecoding logs mean acceptance length ~2.4, per-position 0.64/0.38/0.27/0.16. The same
# box on MTP reads 38.5 (default MTP=2) / 41.2 (speed, MTP=3) in the README tables.
MODE=hybrid
YARN=1
CTX=500000
MTP=0
DRAFT_MODEL=incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2
# K=4 is the measured arm (the acceptance curve is down to ~0.15 by position 4, so the
# trained block-8 depth buys little here); 5-7 now boot too (patch 23 ports the ring
# widening) and are a one-variable benchmark away.
DRAFT_TOKENS=4
# DFlash2 needs the target's FULL vocabulary (the speculators docs reject pruned draft
# vocabularies), so the MTP-head draft-vocab prune (which defaults to on) is disabled here.
# It only ever applied to the MTP head anyway; set explicitly so the serve line reads truthfully.
DRAFT_VOCAB=0
